WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.140
Yo, what's up? How's everyone doing today? First off, welcome to the hackathon. Super excited to

00:05.140 --> 00:10.780
see everyone here and huge shout out to Sunday for bringing us all together. So today is all about

00:10.780 --> 00:15.940
building something cool, experimenting with new ideas, and honestly just having fun with it.

00:16.020 --> 00:23.460
The theme for today's hackathon is 3D simulations on the web using tools like 3.js and AI. And the

00:23.460 --> 00:28.640
idea is pretty simple. Think about something that happens in the real world, figure out how it works,

00:28.640 --> 00:34.260
and bring it to life in your browser. Maybe you want to simulate traffic in Boston, create a crazy

00:34.260 --> 00:38.920
weather system, build a solar system, or have a thousand particles flying around your screen.

00:39.220 --> 00:44.620
Whatever it is, you get to be creative with it. And here's the cool part. With AI coding tools,

00:44.840 --> 00:49.480
you don't have to spend hours figuring out all the complicated physics and math. You can focus

00:49.480 --> 00:54.240
more on your ideas and actually making them happen. Also, don't worry if you've never worked

00:54.240 --> 00:58.160
with 3D before. That's totally fine. This is a place to learn,

00:58.640 --> 01:02.900
try new things, meet cool people, and maybe even build something you didn't think you could build.

01:03.100 --> 01:07.940
And one thing I really want to emphasize is don't overthink it. You don't need to build the most

01:07.940 --> 01:12.660
complicated project in the room. Start with something simple, make it interactive, and see

01:12.660 --> 01:18.020
where it goes. Talk to the people around you, share ideas, ask questions, and don't be afraid

01:18.020 --> 01:22.400
to experiment. By the end of today, hopefully everyone walks away with something cool they've

01:22.400 --> 01:27.320
built, something new they've learned, and maybe a few new friends. So yeah, that's pretty much it.

01:27.460 --> 01:28.620
Huge thanks again to Sunday for bringing us all together. And I'll see you next time.

01:28.640 --> 01:33.140
Thanks to Sunday and to all of you for showing up. I'm really excited to see what everyone comes up with.

